{"text": "MEMO FROM LAURENCE, CHARLES, FREE & LAWSON, INC.\n\nApril 17, 1990 cc: D. Smith\n\nDate: M. DeMato\n\nSubject: Marlboro Ultra Light Test Marketing\nFrom: A. Magnane\n\nTo: Ellen Ashkin\n\n\u2018The following is to provide you with an understanding of Marlboro Ultra Light test\nmarketing to date; packaging, product tipping, media support, etc.\n\nPer Gene Bonnett, Marlboro Ultras are being tested in Indianapolis, Louisville, Ft.\nWayne, Portland, Seattle/Tacoma and Nashville,\n\nT have attached Atco\u2019s Marlboro Ultra December update. It appears this document is\nmissing the Louisville, Ft, Wayne and Seattle/Tacoma data and should be amended.\n\nHere is what we know to date:\nProduct\n\nThree product variations are in test. \u2018The variations are pack colors (2) and tips (2).\n\u2018The constants: T&N\u2019s: 6 mg, tar, 0.5 mg. nicotine. All pack styles: box kings and\n\n100s\nProducts kets\n\u201cBluc\u2019: Blue \"ribbon\" on packs, white tips: Indianapolis, Louisville and Ft,\nWayne.\n\"Red: Red \u201cribbon\u201d on packs, cork tip. Portland, Seattle,\n\"Whi Red \u201cribbon\u201d on packs, white tip: Nashville,\n\nAdvertising Content\n\nA foreground cowboy in four color is shown with a \"ghost\" cowboy montaged behind\nhim. Versions: \"Cowboy and Slicker\", \"Cowboy and Rope\u2019, \"2 Cowboys.\u201d Same copy in\nall advertised markets. Copy: \"New Marlboro Ultra Lights. Now an ultra light good\nenough to be called Marlboro.\u201d Copies attached,", "words": [{"text": "MEMO", "x0": 54, "y0": 39, "x1": 124, "y1": 59, "conf": 94.0}, {"text": "FROM", "x0": 129, "y0": 42, "x1": 188, "y1": 59, "conf": 94.0}, {"text": "LAURENCE,", "x0": 195, "y0": 39, "x1": 318, "y1": 63, "conf": 96.0}, {"text": "CHARLES,", "x0": 324, "y0": 39, "x1": 430, "y1": 63, "conf": 96.0}, {"text": "FREE", "x0": 437, "y0": 40, "x1": 494, "y1": 59, "conf": 93.0}, {"text": "&", "x0": 500, "y0": 40, "x1": 518, "y1": 59, "conf": 93.0}, {"text": "LAWSON,", "x0": 524, "y0": 40, "x1": 